{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/234759-what-do-you-do-to-make-the-game-seem-more-espionagy","id":234759,"title":"What do you do to make the game seem more \"Espionagy\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-19T16:20:16-07:00","id":234759,"title":"What do you do to make the game seem more \"Espionagy\"","content":"What kinds of things do you do to make the game more &quot;Espionagy?&quot; My game is Tecnagostic enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:03:44-07:00","id":234849,"title":"","content":"Uh, it's a game about cover identities under constant surveillance, where your only chance at success and survival is to be well-informed? The game is espionage-y down to the mechanics, IMO; not sure what more you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T12:38:04-07:00","id":235670,"title":"","content":"Start by creating the impetus to hide.The first step of an espionage is the need to hide and be deceptive. An example could be a 3 hunter angels that make routine patrols across the city, threatening compromise rolls fairly regularly. Have obvious infrastructure show up in public places, like the city seal or at city hall, to remind players that their survival requires them to actively work at secrecy. Second, you need to create a need for information. The examples above create a need for the players to learn more. They need to know the Angels, their routes and their capabilities. How far is the G-M embedded in the city political structure? Give the players something tantalizing, or hint at something vital to their safety, and make the information they uncover useful but incomplete. Lastly, I would recommend competition. The players hunt for information, their lives depend on secrecy, but having some other force attempting to claim those same resources will add tension to the game that in inherent to every good spy movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:14:27-07:00","id":235929,"title":"","content":"To add more of this espionage theme in my next session I will start off with one Demon using one of her covers to spy on an angel. The angel kidnapped someone and she is pretending to be a thug who is taking care of him. She is freaking out with the possibility of being spotted, but remember that demons are masters of hiding their feelings. I wil raise the tension when the angel starts interrogating the kidnnaped guy and burn essence to use his powers and she would think he is trying to detect something. In the end I believe she will get an important information about the chronicle and also have a chance to see the angel practicing torture, so I will grow the hate against the villain. <br /> <br /> Other espionage scene is about another demon who is willing to help the players against the God-machine, only to be revealed later that he is part of a nasty russian agency who reports to God-machine another demon's operations just to attract attention while they act at the same time safely. Betrayal in such a hateful way is a common theme in espionage movies, and will make my players to spy on them in order discover who are they and how do they report to the enemy, so they can revenge themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}